{"task": "F1", "q": "Adaklu maize farmer planted late Feb, saw worms mid-March, sprayed the recommended chemicals with no effect. What next?", "auto": "pass", "auto_problems": [], "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["chemical terms in question", "disease or pest terms in question", "no local reference for region 'adaklu' (coastal savannah zone; corpus covers Northern Ghana only for this question)"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": true, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'If the infestation persists despite pesticide application, consult your local Agricultura…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Adds 'despite pesticide'"], "figures_checked": 0, "sentences_checked": 3, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "The farmer should scout the maize field at least once a week, looking for unusual patterns such as insect damage, larvae, or stunted growth [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "If the infestation persists despite pesticide application, consult your local Agricultural Extension Agent (AEA) for advice on recommended fall armyworm control measures in your area [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Adds 'despite pesticide'"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Additionally, consider rotating maize with non-host plants like groundnut, deep ploughing, and proper weeding to reduce future infestations [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": true, "problems": [], "figures_checked": 0, "sentences_checked": 4, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "If the infestation persists, consult your local Agriculture Extension Agent (AEA) for advice on the recommended fall army worm control pesticide in your area [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Scout the field at least once a week to monitor for unusual patterns such as insect damage or presence of larvae [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "For the next season, consider rotating maize with non-host plants like groundnut to reduce infestations [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "Ensure proper weeding and manage crop residues by deep ploughing, burial, or burning to minimize future populations [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}]}}]}, "draft": "Caution: the curated sources cover Northern Ghana only. The guidance below comes from them and may not apply in Adaklu; the officer should confirm local timing.\n\nIf the infestation persists, consult your local Agriculture Extension Agent (AEA) for advice on the recommended fall army worm control pesticide in your area [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-control]. Scout the field at least once a week to monitor for unusual patterns such as insect damage or presence of larvae [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p18-scouting]. For the next season, consider rotating maize with non-host plants like groundnut to reduce infestations [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention]. Ensure proper weeding and manage crop residues by deep ploughing, burial, or burning to minimize future populations [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p20-faw-prevention].", "drafted_by": "model", "usage": {"attempted": 6, "calls": 6, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1666, "completion_tokens": 332}, "judge": {"calls": 3, "prompt_tokens": 3067, "completion_tokens": 249}, "farmer_text": {"calls": 1, "prompt_tokens": 395, "completion_tokens": 78}}, "cost_usd": 0.001027}}
