entence": "Planting should be done after three good rains within the planting window to ensure enough soil moisture [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains].", "cited": ["IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Sow after the rains have stabilized to avoid wilting [MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant].", "cited": ["MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "- Planting should be done between early June and July 10th [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "- Planting can be done from the end of May to early July [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major].", "cited": ["MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 5, "sentence": "- Planting can be done from the end of May to the end of July [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major].", "cited": ["IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 6, "sentence": "Early maturing varieties such as Ewul-Boyu and Wang Dataa can be planted up to the end of July [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'early June' is not in the cited passage(s) ['MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major']", "'July 10th' is not in the cited passage(s) ['MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major']", "'early July' is not in the cited passage(s) ['IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major']", "conflict on maize planting window (APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE, IITA-MAIZE-2025, MOFA-MAIZE) is not shown: [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window]'s own figure is not stated with its own citation", "conflict on maize planting window (APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE, IITA-MAIZE-2025, MOFA-MAIZE) is not shown: [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major]'s own figure is not stated with its own citation", "'Sources give different figures for maize planting window; officer should choose.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Only one source", "'Better yields are achieved with early planting with the first rains.\"  says: \"Major seaso…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No yield info"], "figures_checked": 8, "sentences_checked": 6, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "You can still plant maize in the Northern Region at the end of July, but only if you use early maturing varieties such as Ewul-Boyu and Wang Dataa [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Plant after three good rains within the planting window to ensure enough soil moisture to support germination and early growth [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains].", "cited": ["IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Sow after the rains have stabilized to avoid wilting [MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant].", "cited": ["MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "Sources give different figures for maize planting window; officer should choose.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Only one source"}, {"n": 5, "sentence": "[APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window] says: \"Maize planting in the northern region should be done between early June and July 10th based on the onset of rains.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 6, "sentence": "Better yields are achieved with early planting with the first rains.\" [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major] says: \"Major season | Guinea/Sudan savannah | End of May-early July\" [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major] says: \"Major cropping season | Guinea savannah | End of May - End of July\"", "cited": ["MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major", "IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No yield info"}]}}], "rejected_draft": "You can still plant maize in the Northern Region at the end of July, but only if you use early maturing varieties such as Ewul-Boyu and Wang Dataa [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties]. Plant after three good rains within the planting window to ensure enough soil moisture to support germination and early growth [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains]. Sow after the rains have stabilized to avoid wilting [MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant].\n\nSources give different figures for maize planting window; officer should choose. [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window] says: \"Maize planting in the northern region should be done between early June and July 10th based on the onset of rains. Better yields are achieved with early planting with the first rains.\" [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major] says: \"Major season | Guinea/Sudan savannah | End of May-early July\" [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major] says: \"Major cropping season | Guinea savannah | End of May - End of July\""}, "draft": "[OFFLINE STUB DRAFT - no language model was used; text is assembled from retrieved passages]\nWhat the curated sources say:\n- \"Maize planting in the northern region should be done between early June and July 10th based on the onset of rains. Better yields are achieved with early planting with the first rains.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window]\n- \"It is recommended to plant after three good rains within the planting window to ensure enough soil moisture to support germination and early growth.\" [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains]\n- \"Early maturing varieties such as Ewul-Boyu and Wang Dataa can be planted up to end of July.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties]\n- \"Major season | Guinea/Sudan savannah | End of May-early July\" [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major]\n- \"Major cropping season | Guinea savannah | End of May - End of July\" [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major]\n- \"Planting time or periods differ according to agro-ecology, season and maturity group of the variety. Sow after the rains have stabilized to avoid wilting. Planting time should be informed by local weather information.\" [MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant]\nNote: Sources give different figures for maize planting window; officer should choose.\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.\n\nNote: (officer only) Question received 25 Oct 2026. Windows cited: CSIR-SARI/APNI, northern region: between early June and July 10th; MoFA major season, guinea/sudan savannah: End of May-early July; IITA major season, guinea savannah: End of May - End of July. The date is outside the cited windows.\nNote: (officer only) No rainfall record: rainfall is looked up per district and 'Northern' is not a district AgriReach knows; ask the farmer which district they farm in.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1940, "completion_tokens": 520}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1707, "completion_tokens": 260}}, "cost_usd": 0.000637}}
