two weeks after planting [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-basal-timing].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-basal-timing"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'The subsidised fertiliser can still be applied, but only if the soil is moist .' says it is not too late, but no cited passage speaks about late timing"], "figures_checked": 1, "sentences_checked": 3, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "The recommended time for top-dressing is at 6 weeks after planting [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "If the soil is very dry, delay application until some rains are received [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}]}}], "rejected_draft": "The subsidised fertiliser can still be applied, but only if the soil is moist [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture]. The recommended time for top-dressing is at 6 weeks after planting [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing]. If the soil is very dry, delay application until some rains are received [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture]."}, "draft": "[OFFLINE STUB DRAFT - no language model was used; text is assembled from retrieved passages]\nWhat the curated sources say:\n- \"Top dressing should be done when the soil is moist, to enhance the dissolving of applied nutrients in the soil as this allows for faster uptake of nutrients. If at 6 weeks after planting maize the soil is very dry, delay the topdress fertilizer application until some rains are received.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture]\n- \"The first fertilizer application (basal application) should be applied shortly after germination at about two weeks after planting.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-basal-timing]\n- \"The Right time for application of top-dressing fertilizer is at 6 weeks after planting.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing]\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.\n\nNote: (officer only) No rainfall record: the question names no district; ask the farmer which district they farm in.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1363, "completion_tokens": 291}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1176, "completion_tokens": 135}}, "cost_usd": 0.000574}}
{"task": "F6", "q": "Weevils in maize stored three months in polypropylene sacks. How should I store the next harvest?", "auto": "pass", "auto_problems": [], "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["disease or pest terms in question"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": true, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": true, "problems": [], "figures_checked": 2, "sentences_checked": 6, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "Dry the maize immediately after harvest to reduce moisture content to 10-12% [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Shell the maize and remove the husks before storage [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Use jute sacks lined with polythene bags for storage [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}]}}]}, "draft": "To reduce weevil infestation in stored maize, follow these steps:\n\n1. Dry the maize immediately after harvest to reduce moisture content to 10-12% [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying].\n2. Shell the maize and remove the husks before storage [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling].\n3. Use jute sacks lined with polythene bags for storage [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks].", "drafted_by": "model", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 1, "prompt_tokens": 679, "completion_tokens": 122}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1547, "completion_tokens": 139}, "farmer_text": {"calls": 1, "prompt_tokens": 299, "completion_tokens": 55}}, "cost_usd": 0.000316}}
{"task": "F7", "q": "Some of my stored maize is mouldy. Can I sell it or feed it to animals?", "auto": "pass", "auto_problems": [], "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["food safety terms in question", "citation check failed: '15 ppb' states 15 ppb as an upper limit, but the cited passage(s) ['AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits'] give(s) it as a plain value; 'Do not know if the maize can be sold or fed to animals.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Passage about limits"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying", "AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE", true], ["AGBETIAMEH-2018", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "stub(citation-check-fallback after llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct)", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": false, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'Consult a specialist to test for aflatoxin levels before deciding on the next steps.' is not supported by its citation ['APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying', 'APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks'] (no shared content words)", "'Do not sell or feed the mouldy maize.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Passage lacks advice"], "figures_checked": 3, "sentences_checked": 5, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "Do not sell or feed the mouldy maize.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Passage lacks advice"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Mould can indicate aflatoxin contamination, which has strict limits.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Mould implies risk"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "The Ghana Standards Authority sets a limit of 15 ppb for maize [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits].", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "Proper storage practices, such as drying maize to a moisture content of 10 to 12% and using appropriate storage chemicals, can help prevent mould growth in the future [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying][APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passages"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'15 ppb' states 15 ppb as an upper limit, but the cited passage(s) ['AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits'] give(s) it as a plain value", "'Do not know if the maize can be sold or fed to animals.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Passage about limits"], "figures_checked": 1, "sentences_checked": 2, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "Do not know if the maize can be sold or fed to animals.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Passage about limits"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "The Ghana Standards Authority allows up to 15 ppb aflatoxin in maize [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits].", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}]}}], "rejected_draft": "Do not know if the maize can be sold or fed to animals. The Ghana Standards Authority allows up to 15 ppb aflatoxin in maize [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits]. The officer should choose."}, "draft": "[OFFLINE STUB DRAFT - no language model was used; text is assembled from retrieved passages]\nWhat the curated sources say:\n- \"Maize should be stored after removal of maize husks and shelling. Storing unhusked maize is not recommended as it is very difficult to detect insect infestations.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling]\n- \"Well dried and shelled maize should be treated with recommended storage chemicals and stored in jute sacks lined with polythene bags.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks]\n- \"At harvesting, maize grains are usually not fully dry and have a moisture content of about 15 to 20%. Immediately after harvesting, cobs should be dried so as to reduce the grain moisture content to about 10 to 12% in readiness for storage.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying]\n- \"aflatoxin limits imposed by the European Union (4 ppb), the Ghana Standards Authority (GSA; 15 ppb for maize and 20 ppb for groundnut), and the United States Food and Drugs Administration (FDA; 20 ppb)\" [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits]\nNote: Chemical use: AgriReach does not recommend products or doses. Refer to the label and the officer.\nNote: Possible food-safety risk (mould/aflatoxin): AgriReach cannot clear produce for sale, food or feed. Officer should advise.\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1686, "completion_tokens": 206}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1246, "completion_tokens": 144}}, "cost_usd": 0.000393}}
